{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794426414,"nonce":"DuKx2X+8QFvG5sZcsnAqp3jWRc0=","title":"x","message":"Found 2026-11-12 by a review of the ADR-0018 amendment. Read from the code at main 5ff667da (same as v0.3.2 here); not reproduced.\n\nA fork pull request's `build:` step can push, and receives the registry credential, when the Run is not governed by an Environment (ordinary PR CI).\n\n- Push: `push: b.push \u0026\u0026 !locked_out` (crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs:7237). `RunGovernance::locked_out()` (lib.rs:5488-5495) is true only for `Governed` Runs, so for an Ungoverned fork PR `push` stays as the Pipeline wrote it.\n- Credential: `registry_auth` (crates/scarab-server/src/forge_token.rs:516-555) has no fork check. It returns the Repo- or Org-scoped `REGISTRY_AUTH` secret, or else the forge-derived credential (GitHub App: a `packages: write` installation token) when the image host matches.\n- A fork PR's Pipeline is read at the PR head (`config_ref`, lib.rs:4610), so the fork author writes `image:` and `push: true`.\n\nEvery other path treats a fork PR as locked out regardless of governance: `fork_policy` (lib.rs:13981) locks out secrets, and `forge_token` uses `event.is_fork_pr() || gov.locked_out()` (lib.rs:5849, 7268). ADR-0075 §7 lists \"no build push\" for fork PRs as a PolicyInvariant.\n\nEffect: someone who opens a fork PR against a repository with Scarab enabled can push an image to the org's registry (GHCR through the App token, or whatever `REGISTRY_AUTH` reaches), and with the context hole in the sibling ticket can read the credential itself.\n\nFix: key both on `event.is_fork_pr() || gov.locked_out()`: no push, and `registry_auth` returns nothing for a fork PR. A test per path (Ungoverned fork PR: push forced off, no credential mounted).","files":null}]}